==================================================
8. VERY IMPORTANT — SEND BECOMES STOP
==================================================

This is critical.

When the user sends a message and ChatPop is generating/streaming a response:

The Send button MUST immediately transform into a STOP button.

The stop button should use a square icon.

Use an SF Symbol such as:

"stop.fill"

or a rounded square equivalent.

Example behavior:

Before send:
[ ↑ ]

User taps Send

While AI is responding:
[ ■ ]

After response finishes:
return to normal composer state.

This should happen without layout jump.

The button size and position must remain exactly the same.

Only the icon/state changes.

==================================================
9. STOP BUTTON BEHAVIOR
==================================================

When the user taps the Stop button during generation:

Immediately stop/cancel the current AI response.

Requirements:

- cancel the active streaming/request task
- stop receiving new tokens/content
- keep already-received assistant text visible
- do NOT delete the partial response
- mark the request as stopped/cancelled if needed
- return composer to normal state

If using fetch/streaming on frontend:
use AbortController or the equivalent existing cancellation architecture.

If using native URLSession:
cancel the active URLSessionTask.

If backend supports stream cancellation:
propagate cancellation cleanly.

Do NOT fake the Stop button visually while the request continues running.

It must truly cancel the active request.

==================================================
10. STATE MACHINE
==================================================

Implement the composer using explicit states.

For example:

IDLE_EMPTY
- input empty
- no response generating
- show voice/mic behavior
- send disabled/hidden depending current design

IDLE_WITH_TEXT
- text exists
- no response generating
- show active Send button

SENDING
- request submitted
- immediately switch Send → Stop

STREAMING
- assistant is currently responding
- show Stop button

CANCELLED
- user pressed Stop
- stop stream
- return to idle

COMPLETED
- response finished naturally
- return Stop → normal Send/voice state

ERROR
- response failed
- restore normal composer state
- keep user input/message history intact

Do not allow state inconsistencies.

